OrionLayer open fix 118 — the auto-turn banner on the wire
===========================================================

Work order 403 (package B). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer`
(v2.0.0), on top of open fix 114 and its README row. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp, src/ext/ext_api.h and
src/game/mainscr2.cpp, under ORION2RE_EXT.

With "end of turn wait" off and nothing that needs the player, the engine
runs the next turn by itself: MAINSCR2::Do_Begin_Of_Turn (mainscr2.cpp:
533-596 in the unpatched file) draws the mini main screen with a darkened
box that says the race and the stardate (H 0xE9, "%s stardate %d.%d") and
calls MAINSCR::Do_Next_Turn(&out, 1), which sets in_auto_next_turn_mode,
reads one Get_Input and ends the chain when it returns anything
(mainscr.cpp:2937-2947). MAINSCR::check_next_turn_exit_field is the
engine's own flag that the chain is armed: set in that else branch,
cleared by the first branch and by every way out. None of it was on the
wire.

The change. Do_Begin_Of_Turn hands over what it printed and where
(ext::Auto_Turn_Banner: the text, the box's x, y, w, h) and clears it in
its first branch. SerializeState writes "AUTO" before FILM while the
banner was handed over AND check_next_turn_exit_field holds: uint8 version
(1), uint8 in_auto_next_turn_mode, int16 MOX::global_exit_field (the
whole-screen hidden field with the hotkey ESC that Do_Next_Turn adds while
end_of_turn_wait is 0, mainscr.cpp:2924-2926; 0xFC18 = -1000 when none),
int16 x, y, w, h (native pixels), uint8 n and the n bytes of the text.
Nothing the game reads changes.

The skip is not changed: a click is the whole-screen field's, and ESC
returns -1 (fields.cpp, Interpret_Mouse_Input) whether a field has it or
not; both end the chain through `MOX::auto_turn_exit = Get_Input()`. A
client that wants a click to stop the chain activates that field by its
index or sends ESC.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (work order 403 does not run the engine).
Built on the scratch clone `~/claude/clones/403_orion2re` (`linux-debug`,
ORION2RE_EXT on); a misspelt call (`Auto_Turn_Banner_ClearX`) is refused
by the compiler.

